From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: reset an associated non-AP MLD at a new association

A non-AP MLD that is associated can send a new (Re)Association Request
without a new Authentication, for example a changed request during the
4-way handshake, or a reassociation to the same AP MLD. handle_assoc()
keeps its station entries, so ieee80211_ml_process_link() refuses each
partner link with "MLD: link: Station already exists", and
add_associated_sta() then removes the station from the driver with all
its links. The response refuses the partner links, while hostapd keeps
their entries without a driver station.

IEEE Std 802.11be-2024, 11.3.5.3 l) deletes the states of the earlier
association for a successful association. Reset such a non-AP MLD as
after a timed out SA Query: check the request with a new WPA state
machine, and once hostapd_get_aid() succeeds, free the earlier one and
re-add the station, which removes the entries of the other links. A
non-AP MLD with PMF that is authorized reaches this point only after
its SA Query timed out, because check_sa_query() refuses it before.

The request can come on another link than the association link. Make
the link of the request the association link of the reset, so that the
new state machine takes that link, the re-add replaces the station in
the driver instead of adding a link to the station that it removes, and
the TX status of the response is handled. A refused request restores
the earlier association link.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -7582,6 +7582,7 @@ static void handle_assoc(struct hostapd_
 	bool reset_prev_assoc = false;
 	struct wpa_state_machine *prev_wpa_sm = NULL;
 	struct mld_info prev_mld_info;
+	u8 prev_assoc_link_id = 0;
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
 	if (len < IEEE80211_HDRLEN + (reassoc ? sizeof(mgmt->u.reassoc_req) :
@@ -7823,8 +7824,9 @@ static void handle_assoc(struct hostapd_
 	 * and FILS keep keys of the authentication in the state machine, so
 	 * only Open System and SAE authentication are covered.
 	 */
-	if (hapd->conf->wpa && (sta->flags & WLAN_STA_MFP) &&
-	    sta->sa_query_timed_out && ap_sta_is_mld(hapd, sta) &&
+	if (hapd->conf->wpa && ap_sta_is_mld(hapd, sta) &&
+	    ((sta->flags & WLAN_STA_ASSOC) ||
+	     ((sta->flags & WLAN_STA_MFP) && sta->sa_query_timed_out)) &&
 	    FULL_AP_CLIENT_STATE_SUPP(hapd->iface->drv_flags) &&
 	    (sta->auth_alg == WLAN_AUTH_OPEN ||
 	     sta->auth_alg == WLAN_AUTH_SAE)) {
@@ -7832,6 +7834,9 @@ static void handle_assoc(struct hostapd_
 		prev_wpa_sm = sta->wpa_sm;
 		sta->wpa_sm = NULL;
 		ap_sta_mld_info_copy(&prev_mld_info, &sta->mld_info);
+		/* the link of the request becomes the association link */
+		prev_assoc_link_id = sta->mld_assoc_link_id;
+		sta->mld_assoc_link_id = hapd->mld_link_id;
 	}
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
@@ -7996,8 +8001,10 @@ static void handle_assoc(struct hostapd_
 	}
  fail:
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
-	if (reset_prev_assoc)
+	if (reset_prev_assoc) {
 		ap_sta_restore_wpa_sm(hapd, sta, prev_wpa_sm);
+		sta->mld_assoc_link_id = prev_assoc_link_id;
+	}
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
 	/*
